"""The Fading Firmament's story pass (22 Nov 2026), to docs/quest_writing_standard.md, written after Lastlight was built
and its people moved in: the shrine's people, the magistrate, Orla and the House of Long Memory (moved in from Forgewatch)
all stand in the town; the road's warden, Benedek, the gardener and the quartermaster stay out on the islands. Every
speech is the giver talking from where they now stand; every accept line is a new beat."""

STORY = {
    'ffq_the_road_up': (
        "I write down everyone who comes up the Firmament Road, and the magistrate reads it every evening in Lastlight, just north of here through the town's gate. Three columns of soldiers came up this week, and you. I've kept this post for eleven years, and I've never counted more soldiers than people. Take her the count for me. Tell her I'd like a relief before I start counting the ground going.",
        "She'll ask if I'm eating. Tell her yes, whether it's true or not."),
    'ffq_the_students_trail': (
        "Maelis came to the Firmament before her army did, and she walked it alone, the way she used to walk the Patient Lens's library. I followed her north to find out what she was looking for. Go where she went: the Coldforges' yard north of Lastlight, the rune circle among the Threefold Forge's hearths past them, and over the skip-stone to the Wound's Edge. I taught her to look closely at things. I want to know what she saw.",
        "Look at what's been taken, not what's been left. That's how she always worked."),
    'ffq_the_generals_orders': (
        "Every Siege Legionary on the Siege Line, east of Lastlight, carries a copy of the general's orders under her own seal. I taught Maelis to write when she was nine, so I'll know her hand from across a room. Her orders will say when the fleet sails for the tree. She signs them herself, every copy, because she trusts nobody else's hand. Bring me what they're carrying, and I'll tell you when.",
        "Don't break the seals. I want to see her mark before I read her words."),
    'ffq_the_last_lesson': (
        "Ascendant-General Maelis Ardane stands on the Moorage's pier, north-east of Lastlight, with her fleet's guns round her. I don't want her killed. She's earned a council's judgment, not a quiet end on a pier, and I'd like to be there when she hears it. Break her ward and she'll yield, because she's never fought a fight she'd already lost. Beat her, and bring her back alive.",
        "She's the best the Ascendancy ever had. Bring friends you'd trust with your life."),
    'ffq_columns_on_the_road': (
        "Every column that comes up the road stops outside Lastlight and takes something on the way past: food, crystal, a boy old enough to carry a lance. Since the change they've come every week, and I've watched them take three boys this year. I can't stop them, and I've tried. The Column Legionary and the Column Storm Caller come up past the Road's End, just south of the gate. Meet the next column there, and send it back down.",
        "Let the storm callers come to you. They're weak once they've spent their first bolt."),
    'ffq_the_ones_who_stayed': (
        "Old Benedek Saar was born in his house in the Emptied Quarter, north-west of Lastlight, and he says he'll leave when it does. I've stopped arguing with him, because he's right that it's his house. He's eighty-six and he eats when somebody brings him food. Take him this parcel. Tell him the magistrate says he's still on her books, whether he likes it or not.",
        "He'll try to give you tea. Drink it, he hasn't had a guest in a month."),
    'ffq_scavengers_in_the_quarter': (
        "The houses in the Emptied Quarter are empty, but they're not abandoned. Every family that left meant to come back for what they couldn't carry. Every Ascendancy Scavenger in the Quarter, north-west of Lastlight, strips those houses for anything the fleet can use. Some of the Earthborn here sleep in those houses on the nights they're brave. I keep the roll of every family that left, and I'd like their houses to be there if they come back. Drive the scavengers out of the Quarter.",
        'They work in pairs, one inside and one on the step. Take the one on the step first.'),
    'ffq_word_to_the_council': (
        "The council is going to judge Maelis, and they'll do it without ever having seen the Firmament. I've written it all down: the nine towns, the forges, the ones who stayed and the ones who didn't. It took me four nights by the shrine's light. Take it to First Speaker Aldren Sorvaine in Aurelion yourself. He'll read it if a hero hands it to him.",
        'The last skiff can take you as far as the Bastions. Dorran will wait for you at the ledge.'),
    'ffq_light_for_the_shrine': (
        "The shrine burns light, not oil, and the Firmament is running out of light. Every Fading Wisp drifting between the islands is drinking what's left. I've kept this shrine lit for thirty years, and it's never been this dim. They drift thickest over the Coldforges, out on the Fading Firmament past our gate. Bring me the light they're carrying, and the shrine burns another season.",
        'Hold the light in both hands when you carry it. It leaks through the fingers.'),
    'ffq_over_the_skip_stone': (
        "There's an old skip-stone in the Emptied Quarter, north-west of here, that takes you across the drop to the Wound's Edge. Things are coming up out of the Wound now, the Wound Crawler and the Unmade Wisp, and every week they're nearer the stone. If they cross, they'll be in the Quarter, and then they'll be at our gate. I'd rather they never learned the way. Go over and push them back.",
        'Step off the skip-stone fast. The crawlers wait for people to land.'),
    'ffq_the_unmade': (
        "Since the change, the Wound has grown wider every year. The Edge Gale comes up out of it on the Wound's Edge, north of Lastlight, and tries to throw people off. The old ones here say the Unmade walks the Edge itself, and I've stopped telling them they're wrong. Clear the Edge Gale off, then go and stand there. I'd like to tell the town somebody did.",
        'Plant your feet wide when the gale comes. It only takes people who stand straight.'),
    'ffq_crystals_to_cut': (
        "I'm the last crystal-cutter on the Firmament, and I've got nothing left to cut. Every Ascendancy Cutter up at the Threefold Forge, north of Lastlight, is prising out crystal that's never been burned. They'll ship it to the fleet and burn it in a gun. I could make it into lamps that last a lifetime. Bring me what they've cut out.",
        'Unspent crystal hums when you hold it to your ear. Bring me only the ones that hum.'),
    'ffq_drones_in_the_coldforges': (
        "I was apprenticed in the Coldforges, north of Lastlight, when four of them still burned. Every Salvage Drone there carries the forges' fittings off to the fleet, and every Ascendancy Salvager cuts out the last pieces for them. My master's anvil went last week. I learned to cut my first crystal at that anvil. Stop them, before there's nothing left to remember the forges by.",
        'The drones follow the salvagers. Break the salvagers and the drones just circle.'),
    'ffq_kestrels_on_the_approach': (
        "Mine is the last skiff that still flies out of the Firmament, and every Dusk Kestrel between here and the Bastions has learned it carries food. They go for the sail, and a torn sail up here is a long way down. They nest on the Breaking, out on the Fading Firmament, and hunt the approach to my ledge. I've patched that sail nine times this season. Clear them off the approach, and I'll keep flying.",
        "They dive out of the sunset. Keep it at your back and they can't see you."),
    'ffq_riding_the_dusk_currents': (
        "Two of the Firmament's old wind currents still run, violet now instead of white. One goes out from the Greyfall Gardens, north-west of Lastlight, to an islet with one tree on it. The other goes from the Threefold Forge, far north of here, over to the Dead Engines. Stand where they rise and they'll carry you. I'd go myself, but I'm too old to trust the wind.",
        "Keep your arms in. The current's wider than you are, but only just."),
    'ffq_eels_in_the_lines': (
        "The Breaking sheds rock every day, east of Lastlight, and the Drift Eel follows the rock down. They wrap round my lines when I fly past, and twice this month they've nearly pulled the skiff over. I used to fly the short way home past the Breaking. Clear them out of the gaps round it. I'll take the short way home again.",
        'They hate light. Strike a lamp and they come up out of the gaps to put it out.'),
    'ffq_scrap_that_works': (
        "I ran a scrapyard in Durban for twenty years, and I'd have paid good money for a gear assembly like the ones in a Broken Construct. Up here they're lying all over the Dead Engines, north-east of Lastlight, still turning. The town's water pumps are held together with wire and hope. Bring me the ones that work. I'll keep the pumps running another year.",
        'Shake each one before you take it. If it rattles, leave it for the drones.'),
    'ffq_salvage_the_breaking': (
        "The Breaking is going to fall, east of Lastlight, and everything on it falls too. There's good bronze out there, whole fittings nobody's touched in centuries. The Unmoored Stone and the Hollow Storm won't let me anywhere near it, and I've tried three times. Bronze that old fetches more than gold in Aurelion, and Lastlight needs every coin. Clear the way, and I'll get in and strip what's worth having first.",
        'The stones float. Hit them toward the edge and the drop does the rest.'),
    'ffq_slates_for_the_children': (
        "I taught primary school in Umea before the change, and now I've got eleven children and nothing to write on. There's a school in the Emptied Quarter, north-west of Lastlight, with a cupboard full of slates. The Quarter Sentinel that still guards it won't let anyone carry one out. It doesn't know the children who sat at those desks are gone. Bring me the slates, and I'll teach mine their letters.",
        'Bring chalk if you find any. Slates without chalk are just very sad plates.'),
    'ffq_a_bird_for_the_youngest': (
        "Little Wenna left a toy bird on her front step when her family moved from the Emptied Quarter into Lastlight. She talks about it every night before she sleeps. It's a little bronze bird that floats if you wind it. The Quarter is north-west of here, past the gate, and her old street is the one with the kiosks. I promised her I'd find someone brave enough to look. Go and see if it's still on the step.",
        "If it's there, wind it once before you pick it up. I'd like to know if it still flies."),
    'ffq_three_hearths': (
        "The other houses call the Threefold Forge the Old Forge, and say the Aetherians built it. Look at it properly. One hearth's big enough to stand in, one's set on a perch like a bird's, and one's cut for a smith of our height. Kwabena says no forge where he's from ever had three. The forge is north of Lastlight, past the Coldforges. Look at each hearth closely, then tell me it was built by one people.",
        "Put your hand on each one. They're all warm, and none of them should be."),
    'ffq_below_the_forge': (
        "There's a stair under the Threefold Forge, out on the Fading Firmament, that goes down into the Hearthdeep, where the three flues meet in the stone. Every Ascendancy Salvage-Cutter in the Hearthdeep takes it apart a little more for the fleet. The Flue Guardian wakes up and fights anyone in its flue, cutters and scholars alike. I've waited a thousand years, counting my predecessors, to see the bottom of that stair. Clear the way so my scholars can follow you down.",
        "Don't hurt the guardians if you don't have to. They're the oldest thing down there."),
    'ffq_the_wellspring': (
        "Below the Confluence in the Hearthdeep there's a hall nobody's seen in a thousand years, the Wellspring. The salvage crews went down to cut out what's there, and they woke something. My scholars call it The Unsung, because it howls instead of singing. The way down is under the Threefold Forge, out on the Fading Firmament. Put it down, and let me read what's on the walls.",
        "Cover your ears when it howls. The scholars who didn't still can't hear properly."),
    'ffq_the_seedbed_warden': (
        "There's a spirit in the Wellspring's far seedbeds, deep under the Threefold Forge. Rhun thinks it's a Kharad, still keeping the beds after everyone else went. The Seedbed Warden won't let anyone near them, and I can't blame it for that. I'd like to know what it's been keeping for so long, on the Fading Firmament of all places. Lay it to rest gently, if you can, and let us study the beds.",
        "If it kneels, let it. Rhun says that's how the Kharad said goodbye."),
    'ffq_runes_on_the_guardians': (
        "Every Waking Forge-Guardian at the Threefold Forge, north of Lastlight, is cut with Kharad runes. You can't read a giant's writing standing next to the giant, though. I've tried, and I got a very good look at its knee. Bring me the stones off their shoulders. I'll lay them out on the floor here and read them properly.",
        "The shoulder stones are loose once the guardian falls. Lift them, don't pry."),
    'ffq_the_salvage_master': (
        "Salvage-Master Corin Hask is cutting the cutters' works out of the Hearthdeep piece by piece, benches and racks and all, for the fleet. Those benches are a thousand years old, and they were cut for a smith of our height, which is half of what the Archivist is trying to prove. The way down is under the Threefold Forge, out on the Fading Firmament. He's already had the first bench carried up to the Moorage. Stop him, before there's nothing left down there to read.",
        "He keeps a ledger of what he's taken. Bring it, so we know what to look for in the fleet."),
    'ffq_the_bellows_warden': (
        "The Bellows-Warden stands over the deep anvil at the Confluence, in the Hearthdeep under the Threefold Forge. It pumps air down flues that haven't held a fire in centuries, and it thinks it's keeping the forge alive. I've got to read that anvil, because the Archivist thinks it's the oldest thing the three peoples made together on the Fading Firmament. It won't let me near. Put it down.",
        'It breathes in before it swings. Count the breaths.'),
    'ffq_storms_in_the_flue': (
        "A forge is meant to draw air down, not throw storms up. Every night a Hearth-Bound Storm comes up out of the Threefold Forge's flues, north of Lastlight, and burns whatever the scholars have left up there. I shod horses in Kumasi for fifteen years, and I've never seen a forge that fights back. Put the storms out. Then I'll get on with learning how this thing worked.",
        "Water does nothing to them. Hit them hard and fast, the way you'd beat out a fire."),
    'ffq_the_hollow_engine': (
        "The biggest of the Dead Engines, out on the Fading Firmament, has a hatch at its foot, and inside, there's a machine the size of a town. Something has grown in its burned-out core, black crystal in a lattice, and it attacks anything that comes near. The Black Lattice is all that stands between me and the best engine I'll ever see. I've looked through the hatch, and I could see the gears going down further than my lamp would reach. Kill it, and I'll go in and see how the engine was built.",
        "Break the lattice where it joins the walls. That's where it feeds."),
    'ffq_the_last_governor': (
        "There's a construct in the Hollow Engine's far gallery, the Last Governor, and it's spent centuries trying to start the engine again. Every time it tries, the whole island shakes, and I can feel it in my forge here. Engines are meant to be switched off when they're done, the same as a forge is banked at night. The Hollow Engine's hatch is on the Dead Engines, out on the Fading Firmament. Switch it off before it shakes the island loose.",
        "There's a lever behind its chest plate. If you can reach it, pull it."),
    'ffq_cutters_at_the_door': (
        "I guarded the house's camp at the Threefold Forge until the Archivist moved her rooms into Lastlight. The scholars still go up to the forge every day to work, and I still go with them. Every Ascendancy Cutter up there works right up to where the scholars kneel, cutting crystal out of the hearths. They haven't laid a hand on a scholar yet. Push them back off the forge, north of here, and keep it that way.",
        'Stand between them and the scholars. Cutters are brave until somebody stands in front of them.'),
    'ffq_dead_engine_golems': (
        "The Archivist wants her scholars on the Dead Engines next week, north-east of Lastlight. You get there on the dusk current from the Threefold Forge. Every engine over there has a Dead-Crystal Golem standing at it, and there's a Void-Touched Drifter in every shadow. I've lost one scholar this year, and I'm not losing another. Make it safe enough that I can let them go.",
        'The drifters fade in bright light. Fight them in the open, away from the engines.'),
    'ffq_crawlers_on_my_street': (
        "There's a crack in the street outside my door, and every night a Quarter Crawler comes up out of it. I was born in this house eighty-six years ago, and my father was born in it before me. I'm too old to fight them and too stubborn to leave. Last night one of them got as far as my kitchen. Clear them off my street, and I'll sleep through the night for once.",
        "They come out at dusk. Sit on my step and wait, it's a comfortable step."),
    'ffq_the_family_silver': (
        "They came into my house while I slept and took my mother's silver. An Ascendancy Scavenger has it now, in a sack bound for the fleet. It's six spoons and a little dish, and my mother polished them every Sunday for fifty years. It's no use to anyone but me. Bring it back.",
        'The dish has a dent in it. My brother dropped it in the year the eighth town emptied.'),
    'ffq_ash_off_the_leaves': (
        "Every Ash Puffball in the Greyfall Gardens, south-east of the Last Green, bursts when the wind gets up, and the ash blows out over the drop to my tree. A tree can't breathe through ash. Clear them out of the Gardens before they bury the last green thing on the Firmament. I've wiped every leaf by hand this week, and there are only forty of them left. The Earthborn children at Lastlight call it the Christmas tree, and I haven't the heart to ask them what that means.",
        "Burst them where the wind's blowing away from the drop. The ash goes where the wind goes."),
    'ffq_the_pale_stags': (
        "The stags in the Greyfall Gardens used to be gold, and I remember them running. Now they're pale as the grass, and the Pale Stag eats the bark off anything still standing. If they find the current out to my tree, it's gone, and so is the last green on the Firmament. The Gardens are south-east of here, back across the current. Thin the herd.",
        "Don't take the fawns. The herd can live, as long as it can't reach my tree."),
    'ffq_the_supply_lines': (
        "I fed the Ascendancy for twenty years. I've heard the general call the Earthborn in the Yard Pens a resource, and now I'd like her army to go hungry. Every Bombardier Construct and Vanguard Sky Lancer on the Siege Line guards the crates going north to the Moorage. I packed half those crates myself. Thin the guards out, and the supplies won't get there on time.",
        'The constructs guard the crates, not the road. Go round them and come in from behind.'),
    'ffq_the_supply_ledger': (
        "Every Siege Artillerist on the Siege Line carries a copy of the fleet's supply ledger, so they know what shot to draw. I wrote the first copy myself, and I know exactly what's in it. If the council sees it, they'll know what the general's taking to the tree, and how much. I signed the first page myself, and I'd like to see my name on the evidence. Bring me the copies, and I'll show you.",
        'They keep them in the shot-pouch, not the satchel. Artillerists never trust a satchel.'),
    'ffq_the_vanguard': (
        "The Moorage Marine boards the fleet first, and the Siege Legionary follows. They're the ones who'll land on the tree and hold it while the rest come up. I've seen their landing plan, and it's a good one. They drill on the Siege Line every morning before they march west to the Moorage. Break the vanguard now, and there's nobody to land first.",
        'Hit them while they drill. They stack their shields to the side when they do.'),
    'ffq_the_flagship_wardens': (
        "The general won't leave the Moorage now, not this close to sailing. Her Flagship Wardens hold the gangway, and her Ascendant Battlemages hold the pier. I want the way cleared. If you clear them off, she'll have to come out and see to it herself, because she always does. I'll be there when you face her.",
        "The battlemages shield the wardens. Break the shields first, or you'll be swinging at glass all day."),
}
